# Broadsign

> Broadsign is the leading global platform for managing and monetizing out-of-home (OOH) advertising. Founded in 2003 in Montreal, Canada, Broadsign powers more than 2.8 million static and digital signs across roadways, airports, shopping malls, grocery stores, transit systems, and more in 107 countries. The platform serves over 48 billion ads and 193 billion impressions per month, connecting media owners and buyers through end-to-end software for planning, managing, and transacting OOH media.

## Platform Overview

Broadsign offers two main suites of solutions: one for **media owners and retailers** (to sell, manage, and monetize OOH inventory) and one for **agencies and brands** (to plan, buy, and deliver programmatic DOOH campaigns).

---

## For Media Owners

### Broadsign Platform
The end-to-end solution for media owners to scale, manage, and sell digital and static OOH inventory through automated software, intelligent campaign tools, network operations, and programmatic advertising.
URL: https://broadsign.com/broadsign-platform/

### DOOH Ad Server
Unifies direct and programmatic campaign management into a single workflow. Supports goal-based, slot-based, and programmatic campaign types. Features guaranteed booking with automatic mid-flight rebalancing to ensure delivery. Eliminates the need for multiple platforms and manual spreadsheets.
URL: https://broadsign.com/ad-server/

### Content & Network Management
Manage and automate digital out-of-home media and operations across networks of any size. Features include automated content scheduling (playlist-free), remote network monitoring, proof-of-play reporting, and system-on-chip (SoC) compatibility.
URL: https://broadsign.com/content-network-management/

### Static Campaigns
Centralized asset management and campaign booking tool for static OOH inventory. Syncs with real-time work order status, stock levels, and bill poster communications.
URL: https://broadsign.com/static-campaigns/

### Place Exchange SSP (Global Programmatic SSP)
Broadsign's supply-side platform connects media owners to 55+ DSPs and global omnichannel buyers. Features brand safety filters, automated auctions, strategic pricing tools, and seamless integration into existing tech stacks.
URL: https://broadsign.com/global-programmatic-ssp/

### Local Signage Messaging
Tools for managing locally-relevant content and messaging across OOH networks.
URL: https://broadsign.com/local-signage-messaging/

### Broadsign In-Advance
Automates direct OOH transactions, bringing the speed and ease of programmatic to direct deals. Eliminates the RFP/email back-and-forth between media owners and buyers. Enables automated, guaranteed in-advance deal execution.
URL: https://broadsign.com/broadsign-in-advance/

### System-on-Chip
Broadsign software support for smart screens (SoC devices), enabling network operators to expand compatible hardware.
URL: https://broadsign.com/system-on-chip/

### DOOH more with Broadsign
Broadsign’s flexible selling tools help media owners automate campaign management and rebalancing, enabling them to book 10% more campaigns. By optimizing inventory and filling gaps, owners can drive higher revenue and efficiency.
URL: https://broadsign.com/dooh-more/

